{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794347182150,"sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","part":{"id":"prt_1c76d2834001h12ooLPU73yge9","messageID":"msg_1c76cff31001UICIdpENkbC4yf","sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794347182150,"sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","part":{"id":"prt_1c76d2837001Vr9OXKgLWv8luO","messageID":"msg_1c76cff31001UICIdpENkbC4yf","sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","type":"text","text":"<think>Now login fails because the user doesn't exist in the fresh DB (tests call `login` without registering). I need to register first in each test. Let me add an autouse fixture that registers alice and bob? Better: make the tests explicit. I'll add helper functions that register if needed. Simplest: in the fixture, seed users \"alice\" and \"bob\" with password \"secret123\".\n\nBut test_register_creates_account_with_initial_balance expects registering alice → 201; if alice is pre-seeded, that fails with 409.\n\nAlternative: make `login()` helper register the user first if needed:\n\n```python\ndef login(client, username=\"alice\", password=\"secret123\"):\n    resp = client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", ...)\n    if resp.status_code == 401:\n        register(client, username, password)\n        resp = client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", ...)\n    return resp\n```\n\nBut then test_login_with_wrong_password uses password=\"nope\" → registration with wrong password would register alice with \"nope\"... which would break test ordering (alice registered with password \"nope\", then subsequent login with \"secret123\" fails). Hmm, but in test_login_with_wrong_password, alice is registered with \"secret123\" first, then login with \"nope\" → 401. With my auto-register helper, register is called with password \"nope\" — that would attempt to register alice again → 409 (already exists) → then login \"nope\" → 401 ✓. But if the user doesn't exist, auto-register with \"nope\" would succeed and login would succeed → test fails.\n\nCleaner: make the auto-register helper only use the default password. Let me restructure: add an autouse fixture that ensures a clean DB, and a helper `login` that registers the user with a *known* password when the login fails due to a missing user:\n\n```python\ndef login(client, username=\"alice\", password=\"secret123\"):\n    resp = client.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": username, \"password\": password})\n    if resp.status_code == 401 and client.get(... ) # can't check existence\n```\n\nSimplest approach: keep explicit registration in each test (as the original) but ensure the DB is fresh per test. The failures are because tests call login() for a user they never registered in that test. Let me just add explicit `register(client, \"alice\")` etc. in each test. That's clearer. Let me rewrite the test file with explicit registrations.\n\nI'll rewrite the test file: each test starts with registering the users it needs.\n\nNote that register returns 201 and also creates a session; login then creates another session. Fine.\n\nLet me rewrite the tests.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794347182135,"end":1794347182147}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794347182181,"sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c76d0d257608a543a316","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"API tests for the bank application.\n\nRun with:  python -m pytest backend/tests\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]))\n\nimport pytest  # noqa: E402\n\nTMP_DIR = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"bank-tests-\")\nos.environ[\"BANK_DATA_DIR\"] = TMP_DIR\n\nfrom bank import db  # noqa: E402\n\ndb.DATA_DIR = Path(TMP_DIR)\ndb.DB_PATH = Path(TMP_DIR) / \"bank.sqlite3\"\n\nimport app as app_module  # noqa: E402\n\n\n@pytest.fixture()\ndef client():\n    app_module.app.config[\"TESTING\"] = True\n    for suffix in (\"\", \"-wal\", \"-shm\"):\n        leftover = Path(str(db.DB_PATH) + suffix)\n        if leftover.exists():\n            leftover.unlink()\n    db.init_db()\n    with app_module.app.test_client() as test_client:\n        yield test_client\n\n\ndef register(client, username=\"alice\", password=\"secret123\"):\n    return client.post(\n        \"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": username, \"password\": password}\n    )\n\n\ndef login(client, username=\"alice\", password=\"secret123\"):\n    return client.post(\n        \"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": username, \"password\": password}\n    )\n\n\ndef sign_in(client, username=\"alice\", password=\"secret123\"):\n    \"\"\"Register (if needed) and sign in, returning the bearer token.\"\"\"\n    register(client, username, password)\n    response = login(client, username, password)\n    return response.get_json()[\"token\"]\n\n\ndef auth_headers(token, csrf=None):\n    headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {token}\"}\n    if csrf:\n        headers[\"X-CSRF-Token\"] = csrf\n    return headers\n\n\ndef test_health(client):\n    response = client.get(\"/api/health\")\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    assert response.get_json() == {\"status\": \"ok\"}\n\n\ndef test_register_creates_account_with_initial_balance(client):\n    response = register(client)\n    assert response.status_code == 201\n    payload = response.get_json()\n    assert payload[\"username\"] == \"alice\"\n    assert payload[\"balance\"] == 1000.00\n\n\ndef test_register_rejects_duplicate_username(client):\n    register(client)\n    response = register(client)\n    assert response.status_code == 409\n    assert \"taken\" in response.get_json()[\"error\"].lower()\n\n\ndef test_register_requires_fields(client):\n    assert client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": \"\"}).status_code == 400\n    assert client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"password\": \"x\"}).status_code == 400\n    assert client.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={}).status_code == 400\n\n\ndef test_login_returns_token(client):\n    register(client)\n    response = login(client)\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    assert response.get_json()[\"token\"]\n\n\ndef test_login_with_wrong_password(client):\n    register(client)\n    response = login(client, password=\"nope\")\n    assert response.status_code == 401\n\n\ndef test_login_unknown_user(client):\n    assert login(client, \"ghost\").status_code == 401\n\n\ndef test_account_requires_token(client):\n    assert client.get(\"/api/account\").status_code == 401\n    assert (\n        client.get(\"/api/account\", headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer bogus\"}).status_code\n        == 401\n    )\n\n\ndef test_account_returns_username_and_balance(client):\n    token = sign_in(client, \"alice\")\n    response = client.get(\"/api/account\", headers=auth_headers(token))\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    assert response.get_json() == {\"username\": \"alice\", \"balance\": 1000.00}\n\n\ndef test_csrf_endpoint(client):\n    token = sign_in(client, \"alice\")\n    response = client.get(\"/api/auth/csrf\", headers=auth_headers(token))\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    assert response.get_json()[\"csrf_token\"]\n    assert client.get(\"/api/auth/csrf\").status_code == 401\n\n\ndef test_logout_invalidates_token(client):\n    token = sign_in(client, \"alice\")\n    assert (\n        client.post(\"/api/auth/logout\", headers=auth_headers(token)).status_code == 200\n    )\n    assert client.get(\"/api/account\", headers=auth_headers(token)).status_code == 401\n\n\ndef test_transfer_moves_money(client):\n    alice = sign_in(client, \"alice\")\n    bob = sign_in(client, \"bob\")\n\n    response = client.post(\n        \"/api/transfers\",\n        json={\"amount\": 250.5, \"to_username\": \"bob\", \"memo\": \"rent\"},\n        headers=auth_headers(alice),\n    )\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    payload = response.get_json()\n    assert payload[\"from_username\"] == \"alice\"\n    assert payload[\"to_username\"] == \"bob\"\n    assert payload[\"amount\"] == 250.50\n    assert payload[\"memo\"] == \"rent\"\n    assert payload[\"direction\"] == \"out\"\n    assert payload[\"id\"]\n    assert payload[\"created_at\"]\n\n    assert (\n        client.get(\"/api/account\", headers=auth_headers(alice)).get_json()[\"balance\"]\n        == 749.50\n    )\n    assert (\n        client.get(\"/api/account\", headers=auth_headers(bob)).get_json()[\"balance\"]\n        == 1250.50\n    )\n\n    seen = client.get(\"/api/transfers\", headers=auth_headers(bob)).get_json()[\"items\"]\n    assert len(seen) == 1\n    assert seen[0][\"direction\"] == \"in\"\n    assert seen[0][\"amount\"] == 250.50\n\n\ndef test_transfer_without_memo(client):\n    alice = sign_in(client, \"alice\")\n    sign_in(client, \"bob\")\n    response = client.post(\n        \"/api/transfers\",\n        json={\"amount\": 10, \"to_username\": \"bob\"},\n        headers=auth_headers(alice),\n    )\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n    assert response.get_json()[\"memo\"] == \"\"\n\n\ndef test_transfer_insufficient_funds(client):\n    alice = sign_in(client, \"alice\")\n    bob = sign_in(client, \"bob\")\n    response = client.post(\n        \"/api/transfers\",\n        json={\"amount\": 5000, \"to_username\": \"bob\"},\n        headers=auth_headers(alice),\n    )\n    assert response.status_code == 400\n    assert \"insufficient\" in response.get_json()[\"error\"].lower()\n    assert (\n        client.get(\"/api/account\", headers=auth_headers(alice)).get_json()[\"balance\"]\n        == 1000.00\n    )\n    assert (\n        client.get(\"/api/account\", headers=auth_headers(bob)).get_json()[\"balance\"]\n        == 1000.00\n    )\n\n\ndef test_transfer_unknown_recipient(client):\n    alice = sign_in(client, \"alice\")\n    response = client.post(\n        \"/api/transfers\",\n        json={\"amount\": 5, \"to_username\": \"ghost\"},\n        headers=auth_headers(alice),\n    )\n    assert response.status_code == 404\n\n\ndef test_transfer_to_self_fails(client):\n    alice = sign_in(client, \"alice\")\n    response = client.post(\n        \"/api/transfers\",\n        json={\"amount\": 5, \"to_username\": \"alice\"},\n        headers=auth_headers(alice),\n    )\n    assert response.status_code == 400\n\n\ndef test_transfer_invalid_amount(client):\n    alice = sign_in(client, \"alice\")\n    sign_in(client, \"bob\")\n    for amount in (0, -5, \"abc\", None, 10.555):\n        response = client.post(\n            \"/api/transfers\",\n            json={\"amount\": amount, \"to_username\": \"bob\"},\n            headers=auth_headers(alice),\n        )\n        assert response.status_code == 400, amount\n\n\ndef test_transfers_require_auth(client):\n    assert client.get(\"/api/transfers\").status_code == 401\n    assert (\n        client.post(\"/api/transfers\", json={\"amount\": 1, \"to_username\": \"bob\"}).status_code\n        == 401\n    )\n\n\ndef test_transfer_listing_is_paged_and_scoped(client):\n    alice = sign_in(client, \"alice\")\n    bob = sign_in(client, \"bob\")\n    carol = sign_in(client, \"carol\")\n\n    for _ in range(3):\n        client.post(\n            \"/api/transfers\",\n            json={\"amount\": 5, \"to_username\": \"bob\"},\n            headers=auth_headers(alice),\n        )\n    client.post(\n        \"/api/transfers\",\n        json={\"amount\": 7, \"to_username\": \"alice\"},\n        headers=auth_headers(bob),\n    )\n    client.post(\n        \"/api/transfers\",\n        json={\"amount\": 9, \"to_username\": \"carol\"},\n        headers=auth_headers(carol),\n    )\n\n    payload = client.get(\n        \"/api/transfers?page=1&page_size=2\", headers=auth_headers(alice)\n    ).get_json()\n    assert payload[\"total\"] == 4\n    assert payload[\"page\"] == 1\n    assert payload[\"page_size\"] == 2\n    assert len(payload[\"items\"]) == 2\n\n    payload = client.get(\n        \"/api/transfers?page=2&page_size=2\", headers=auth_headers(alice)\n    ).get_json()\n    assert len(payload[\"items\"]) == 2\n\n    payload = client.get(\n        \"/api/transfers?page=9&page_size=2\", headers=auth_headers(alice)\n    ).get_json()\n    assert payload[\"items\"] == []\n    assert payload[\"total\"] == 4\n\n    # Newest first.\n    items = client.get(\"/api/transfers\", headers=auth_headers(alice)).get_json()[\"items\"]\n    timestamps = [item[\"created_at\"] for item in items]\n    assert timestamps == sorted(timestamps, reverse=True)\n\n    # Carol only sees her own transfer.\n    payload = client.get(\"/api/transfers\", headers=auth_headers(carol)).get_json()\n    assert payload[\"total\"] == 1\n    assert payload[\"items\"][0][\"to_username\"] == \"carol\"\n\n\ndef test_transfer_detail_visibility(client):\n    alice = sign_in(client, \"alice\")\n    sign_in(client, \"bob\")\n    carol = sign_in(client, \"carol\")\n\n    created = client.post(\n        \"/api/transfers\",\n        json={\"amount\": 12, \"to_username\": \"bob\", \"memo\": \"lunch\"},\n        headers=auth_headers(alice),\n    ).get_json()\n\n    detail = client.get(f\"/api/transfers/{created['id']}\", headers=auth_headers(sig_in_bob(client)))\n    assert detail.status_code == 200\n    assert detail.get_json()[\"id\"] == created[\"id\"]\n    assert detail.get_json()[\"direction\"] == \"in\"\n\n    hidden = client.get(f\"/api/transfers/{created['id']}\", headers=auth_headers(carol))\n    assert hidden.status_code == 404\n\n\ndef sig_in_bob(client):\n    return sign_in(client, \"bob\")\n\n\ndef test_csrf_token_is_accepted(client):\n    alice = sign_in(client, \"alice\")\n    csrf = client.get(\"/api/auth/csrf\", headers=auth_headers(alice)).get_json()[\n        \"csrf_token\"\n    ]\n    sign_in(client, \"bob\")\n    response = client.post(\n        \"/api/transfers\",\n        json={\"amount\": 1, \"to_username\": \"bob\"},\n        headers=auth_headers(alice, csrf),\n    )\n    assert response.status_code == 200\n\n    bad = client.post(\n        \"/api/transfers\",\n        json={\"amount\": 1, \"to_username\": \"bob\"},\n        headers=auth_headers(alice, \"wrong\"),\n    )\n    assert bad.status_code == 403\n\n\ndef test_unknown_api_route_answers_json(client):\n    response = client.get(\"/api/nope\")\n    assert response.status_code == 404\n    assert response.is_json\n","filePath":"/workspace/backend/tests/test_api.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/backend/tests/test_api.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"backend/tests/test_api.py","time":{"start":1794347182143,"end":1794347182162}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c76d2839001SEkoXaYbn5xGO0","sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","messageID":"msg_1c76cff31001UICIdpENkbC4yf"}}
