{"type":"text","timestamp":1794347204183,"sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","part":{"id":"prt_1c76d7e4b0018vum1qy64pZGZk","messageID":"msg_1c76d46530018kI2x0C3bNfR1q","sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","type":"text","text":"<think>Carol's total is 0 — because bob→alice and carol→carol? Wait: `client.post(\"/api/transfers\", json={\"amount\": 9, \"to_username\": \"carol\"}, headers=auth_headers(carol))` — carol transfers to herself → 400 error. My test was wrong: it should be carol → alice or alice → carol. Let me fix the test: carol sends to alice.\n\nThen carol's total = 1 (her sent transfer) ✓. But alice's total would become 5 (3 + 1 received from bob + 1 received from carol). Let me restructure: carol sends 9 to bob → carol total 1, bob total = 3 received + 1 from alice? Let me just make carol send to alice: alice receives from bob (7) and from carol (9) → alice total = 3 sent + 2 received = 5.\n\nLet me update: alice total == 5, page_size 2 → page 1: 2 items, page 2: 2 items, page 3: 1 item, page 9: empty. Carol total = 1.\n\nLet me updatethe test.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794347204171,"end":1794347204181}}}
