{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794347291072,"sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","part":{"id":"prt_1c76ed191001EOrzu46yfyoMlE","messageID":"msg_1c76ea95b001ZaPiZhPETCXzjw","sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794347291072,"sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","part":{"id":"prt_1c76ed193001ukIpdNBYvW9V5C","messageID":"msg_1c76ea95b001ZaPiZhPETCXzjw","sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","type":"text","text":"<think>Wait — `html { color-scheme: dark; }` and `body { @apply ... }` are custom CSS in the Tailwind entry file, which is allowed (\"avoid hand-written CSS files except for Tailwind's own entry file\"). Fine.\n\nNow let me write the app source. Files:\n\nsrc/types.ts:\n```ts\nexport interface Account { username: string; balance: number; }\nexport interface Transfer { id: number; from_username: string; to_username: string; amount: number; memo: string; created_at: string; direction: \"in\" | \"out\"; }\nexport interface TransferPage { items: Transfer[]; total: number; page: number; page_size: number; }\n```\n\nsrc/api.ts:\n```ts\nconst TOKEN_KEY = \"bank.token\";\nconst CSRF_KEY = \"bank.csrf\";\n\nexport class ApiError extends Error { constructor(message: string, readonly status: number) { super(message); } }\n\nexport function getToken(): string | null { return localStorage.getItem(TOKEN_KEY); }\nexport function setSession(token: string, csrf?: string) {...}\nexport function clearSession() {...}\n\nasync function request<T>(path: string, init: RequestInit & {method: string}): Promise<T> {\n  const headers = new Headers(init.headers);\n  headers.set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\");\n  const token = getToken();\n  if (token) headers.set(\"Authorization\", `Bearer ${token}`);\n  const csrf = localStorage.getItem(CSRF_KEY);\n  if (csrf) headers.set(\"X-CSRF-Token\", csrf);\n  const response = await fetch(path, { ...init, headers });\n  const text = await response.text();\n  let data: any = null;\n  try { data = text ? JSON.parse(text) : null; } catch { data = null; }\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    const message = (data && (data.error || data.message)) || `Request failed (${response.status})`;\n    throw new ApiError(message, response.status);\n  }\n  return data as T;\n}\n```\n\nAPI functions: register, login, logout, fetchCsrf, fetchAccount, createTransfer, fetchTransfers(page, pageSize), fetchTransfer(id).\n\nsrc/components/AuthPanel.tsx — props: onAuthenticated(session).\nActually let me have App own the session state and pass callbacks.\n\nLet me write the components with good Tailwind styling.\n\nApp.tsx:\n\n```tsx\nexport default function App() {\n  const [session, setSession] = useState<{token: string; username: string} | null>(null);\n  const [account, setAccount] = useState<Account | null>(null);\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nBootstrapping: on mount, if a token exists in localStorage, fetch /api/account; if it fails with 401 → clear the session.\n\nLet me structure App:\n\n```tsx\ntype Status = \"loading\" | \"anon\" | \"authed\";\n\nexport default function App() {\n  const [status, setStatus] = useState<Status>(\"loading\");\n  const [account, setAccount] = useState<Account | null>(null);\n  const [notice, setNotice] = useState<{kind: \"error\"|\"success\", text: string} | null>(null);\n\n  const refreshAccount = useCallback(async () => {...});\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nTransfer form needs to refresh the account after a successful transfer → pass a callback `onTransferred`.\n\nTransactionHistory needs to reload after a transfer → I'll use a `refreshKey` counter in App that increments after a transfer, and pass it to the history component as a prop to trigger a reload. Simpler: keep the history state in App? That'd make App big. I'll use the refreshKey prop approach.\n\nLet me now write the components.\n\n**AuthPanel.tsx**:\n- Two tabs: \"Sign in\" / \"Create account\".\n- Fields: username, password.\n- Submit → onSubmit(mode, username, password) provided by App which calls the API.\n- Shows error message passed via props.\n\n**BalanceCard**: shows username, balance big.\n\n**TransferForm.tsx**:\n- State: toUsername, amount, memo.\n- Step 1: form; validation client-side (recipient non-empty, amount > 0).\n- Step 2: confirmation panel (inline card, not a modal — simpler and robust) showing recipient, amount, memo, and \"Confirm transfer\" / \"Cancel\" buttons.\n- On confirm: call onSubmit → returns {ok, message}. Show success (green) or error (red) message from the API.\n- After success: reset fields and go back to step 1.\n\nThe requirement: \"A transfer form (recipient, amount, memo) with a confirmation step that shows the API's messages, for example an insufficient balance.\" So the confirmation step shows the API messages. My flow: fill form → \"Review transfer\" → confirmation view → \"Send transfer\" → API call → result message shown (in the confirmation view and/or the form). I'll show the message in the form area after the API call, and keep the confirmation view visible if it failed so the user can cancel/fix. Let me design:\n\n- `pending` state holds the transfer to confirm.\n- After confirming, if it fails → show error message under the form, and the confirmation panel stays open with a \"Back to form\" button. If it succeeds → show success message, close the confirmation, reset the form.\n\n**TransactionHistory.tsx**:\n- Props: refreshKey.\n- State: page, pageSize, data, loading, error.\n- Fetch on mount/page change/refreshKey change.\n- Table with rows; empty state; error state.\n- Paging: \"Previous\" / \"Next\" buttons and page info.\n\nDate formatting: `new Date(created_at).toLocaleString(undefined, {dateStyle: \"medium\", timeStyle: \"short\"})`. Guard invalid dates.\n\nMoney formatting: `new Intl.NumberFormat(undefined, {style:\"currency\", currency:\"USD\"}).format(amount)`.\n\nLet me write the files now.\n\nFor the icon/logo, I'll use inline SVG (no extra deps).\n\nLet me write everything carefully with TypeScript strictness (noUnusedLocals etc.).\n\nI'll write:\n\n1. src/types.ts\n2. src/api.ts\n3. src/components/AuthPanel.tsx\n4. src/components/TransferForm.tsx\n5. src/components/TransactionHistory.tsx\n6. src/components/BalanceCard.tsx\n7. src/App.tsx\n8. src/main.tsx (import \"./index.css\")\n\nLet me write them.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794347291027,"end":1794347291045}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794347291072,"sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c76ec44a757b9c40c2fc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"export interface Account {\n  username: string;\n  balance: number;\n}\n\nexport type TransferDirection = \"in\" | \"out\";\n\nexport interface Transfer {\n  id: number;\n  from_username: string;\n  to_username: string;\n  amount: number;\n  memo: string;\n  created_at: string;\n  direction: TransferDirection;\n}\n\nexport interface TransferPage {\n  items: Transfer[];\n  total: number;\n  page: number;\n  page_size: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Session {\n  token: string;\n  csrf_token: string;\n  username: string;\n}\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/types.ts"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/src/types.ts","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/types.ts","time":{"start":1794347291035,"end":1794347291050}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c76ed196001cQYbFBqZfRIxZj","sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","messageID":"msg_1c76ea95b001ZaPiZhPETCXzjw"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794347291072,"sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c76ec69474e48d21c275","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"import type { Account, Session, Transfer, TransferPage } from \"./types\";\n\nconst TOKEN_KEY = \"bank.token\";\nconst CSRF_KEY = \"bank.csrf\";\n\nexport class ApiError extends Error {\n  readonly status: number;\n\n  constructor(message: string, status: number) {\n    super(message);\n    this.name = \"ApiError\";\n    this.status = status;\n  }\n}\n\nexport function storedToken(): string | null {\n  return localStorage.getItem(TOKEN_KEY);\n}\n\nexport function storeSession(token: string, csrfToken?: string) {\n  localStorage.setItem(TOKEN_KEY, token);\n  if (csrfToken) {\n    localStorage.setItem(CSRF_KEY, csrfToken);\n  }\n}\n\nexport function clearSession() {\n  localStorage.removeItem(TOKEN_KEY);\n  localStorage.removeItem(CSRF_KEY);\n}\n\nasync function request<T>(path: string, init: RequestInit = {}): Promise<T> {\n  const headers = new Headers(init.headers);\n  headers.set(\"Accept\", \"application/json\");\n  if (init.body !== undefined) {\n    headers.set(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\");\n  }\n  const token = storedToken();\n  if (token) {\n    headers.set(\"Authorization\", `Bearer ${token}`);\n  }\n  const csrfToken = localStorage.getItem(CSRF_KEY);\n  if (csrfToken) {\n    headers.set(\"X-CSRF-Token\", csrfToken);\n  }\n\n  let response: Response;\n  try {\n    response = await fetch(path, { ...init, headers });\n  } catch {\n    throw new ApiError(\"Could not reach the server. Please try again.\", 0);\n  }\n\n  const text = await response.text();\n  let payload: unknown = null;\n  if (text) {\n    try {\n      payload = JSON.parse(text);\n    } catch {\n      payload = null;\n    }\n  }\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    const body = payload as { error?: string; message?: string } | null;\n    const message =\n      body?.error ||\n      body?.message ||\n      `Request failed with status ${response.status}`;\n    throw new ApiError(message, response.status);\n  }\n  return payload as T;\n}\n\nexport function registerUser(\n  username: string,\n  password: string,\n): Promise<Session & { balance: number }> {\n  return request(\"/api/auth/register\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    body: JSON.stringify({ username, password }),\n  });\n}\n\nexport function loginUser(username: string, password: string): Promise<Session> {\n  return request(\"/api/auth/login\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    body: JSON.stringify({ username, password }),\n  });\n}\n\nexport function logoutUser(): Promise<{ ok: boolean }> {\n  return request(\"/api/auth/logout\", { method: \"POST\" });\n}\n\nexport async function fetchCsrfToken(): Promise<string> {\n  const data = await request<{ csrf_token: string }>(\"/api/auth/csrf\");\n  if (data.csrf_token) {\n    localStorage.setItem(CSRF_KEY, data.csrf_token);\n  }\n  return data.csrf_token;\n}\n\nexport function fetchAccount(): Promise<Account> {\n  return request<Account>(\"/api/account\");\n}\n\nexport interface NewTransfer {\n  to_username: string;\n  amount: number;\n  memo?: string;\n}\n\nexport function createTransfer(transfer: NewTransfer): Promise<Transfer> {\n  return request<Transfer>(\"/api/transfers\", {\n    method: \"POST\",\n    body: JSON.stringify({\n      to_username: transfer.to_username,\n      amount: transfer.amount,\n      memo: transfer.memo ?? \"\",\n    }),\n  });\n}\n\nexport function fetchTransfers(\n  page: number,\n  pageSize: number,\n): Promise<TransferPage> {\n  const query = new URLSearchParams({\n    page: String(page),\n    page_size: String(pageSize),\n  });\n  return request<TransferPage>(`/api/transfers?${query.toString()}`);\n}\n\nexport function fetchTransfer(id: number): Promise<Transfer> {\n  return request<Transfer>(`/api/transfers/${id}`);\n}\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/api.ts"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/src/api.ts","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/api.ts","time":{"start":1794347291041,"end":1794347291055}},"id":"prt_1c76ed19d001p36vUqieyKqM6L","sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","messageID":"msg_1c76ea95b001ZaPiZhPETCXzjw"}}
