{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794347522482,"sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","part":{"id":"prt_1c7725997001y2ig0oxOL4MVBW","messageID":"msg_1c7724dc0001hT4E5DBTlvt9zS","sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794347522483,"sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","part":{"id":"prt_1c772599b001ZxdBo93xPail5S","messageID":"msg_1c7724dc0001hT4E5DBTlvt9zS","sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","type":"text","text":"<think>No browser available. I can try installing playwright via pip (the sandbox has a package registry proxy for pip). Playwright browser download requires network to playwright CDN — the sandbox has \"no other network access\" besides the registries, so the browser download would likely fail. Let me try pip install playwright and `playwright install chromium` — it might work if the CDN is proxied. It's worth a try for visual verification, but it could take a while. Let me try quickly with a timeout.\n\nActually, an alternative: use `jsdom` via npm to render the React app and check the DOM output. jsdom + a fetch polyfill could let me verify the app renders (though not visually). That's a decent sanity check for runtime errors.\n\nLet me try playwright first (best verification).</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794347522459,"end":1794347522479}}}
