{"type":"text","timestamp":1794347551887,"sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","part":{"id":"prt_1c772cc7c0015VLbA4MBB3Wboi","messageID":"msg_1c772c2ec001j1n9OOY4JUeobN","sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","type":"text","text":"<think>External directories other than /tmp/opencode are denied. /tmp/opencode exists but isn't writable by my user (owned by root, 755). Let me check if I can create a subdirectory inside it... \"drwxr-xr-x 2 root root\" → not writable.\n\nHmm. But the rule allows /tmp/opencode/* patterns. The filesystem permission denies writing though. Let me test writing there.\n\nAlternative: create the scratch dir inside /workspace (e.g. /workspace/.scratch) and delete it afterwards. That's within the workspace, so allowed. I'll clean it up at the end and make sure it isn't committed.\n\nLet me do that.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794347551868,"end":1794347551883}}}
