{"type":"text","timestamp":1794347623032,"sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","part":{"id":"prt_1c773e26c001DyF6Iej6DNAzQL","messageID":"msg_1c773d6d7001JtrtFrx2YmbSo8","sessionID":"ses_e38957fc2ffea5rGdpZf5rJULa","type":"text","text":"<think>The dev build references `process.env.NODE_ENV`. I need to define `process` in the jsdom window, or build in production mode. Let me set `process` in the window before eval:\n\n```js\nwindow.process = { env: { NODE_ENV: \"production\" } };\n```\n\nBut React's dev build checks process.env.NODE_ENV at runtime — with \"production\" it uses the production bundle. Good. Let me also set `window.process` = globalThis.process? That would give process.env.NODE_ENV = undefined → React dev mode. Setting NODE_ENV=\"production\" is better.\n\nLet me add that.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794347623020,"end":1794347623030}}}
